00:37:14.622 --> 00:37:17.080
So we looked at the demo from
three different perspectives.

00:37:17.080 --> 00:37:19.480
We looked at how the
application developer or API

00:37:19.480 --> 00:37:22.642
consumer was able to
easily go out to a portal,

00:37:22.642 --> 00:37:24.100
learn everything
that was required,

00:37:24.100 --> 00:37:26.950
get credentials, and start
building an application

00:37:26.950 --> 00:37:28.703
and sending in
traffic very quickly.

00:37:28.703 --> 00:37:30.370
The amount of friction
required to build

00:37:30.370 --> 00:37:32.470
that first step is very low.

00:37:32.470 --> 00:37:35.380
We saw how the API developer
took an existing service,

00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:37.540
and started to manage
it with Apigee,

00:37:37.540 --> 00:37:39.490
and put some products
in place so it

00:37:39.490 --> 00:37:42.040
was easy for these
